('kas-001', 'Working on redundant trains: the second check', 'العمل على المسارات الاحتياطية: التحقق الثاني', 'Why a peer check at the local panel is the real defence when two redundant trains are open for work, and how to set up the job so the layout points to the right train.', 'لماذا يُعد التحقق من الزميل عند اللوحة المحلية الدفاع الحقيقي حين يُفتح مساران احتياطيان للعمل، وكيف يُهيأ العمل بحيث يدل المكان على المسار الصحيح.', 'We had two redundant trains of the component cooling pumps opened for work in the same week, and the work packages looked almost identical. The labels on the pump skids were faded on train B, so the only real defence was the second check. My rule of thumb: before you put a hand on redundant equipment, stop at the local panel, read the component number aloud, and have your partner read it from the work order, not from memory. The time it costs is less than a minute. The time it saves is a forced outage or worse. We also learned to stage the tools on the correct train the day before, so the physical setup itself points you to the right place. When a newcomer asks why we are slow, I tell them the peer check is the job, not a delay to the job. Look at the operating experience on the wrong-train event; it is the same story every time: a confident person, a familiar layout, and one missing check.', 'en', '[{"en":"Read the component number aloud at the local panel; your partner reads it from the work order.","ar":"اقرأ رقم المكوّن بصوت مسموع عند اللوحة المحلية، ويقرأه زميلك من أمر العمل."},{"en":"Stage tools on the correct train the day before.","ar":"جهّز الأدوات على المسار الصحيح في اليوم السابق."},{"en":"The peer check is the job, not a delay to the job.","ar":"التحقق من الزميل جزء من العمل وليس تأخيراً له."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-mp-01-mech','sk-hu-01','sk-mp-01']::text[], array['qs-mech']::text[], array['qs-mech']::text[], array['oe-1']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'maintenance', 'published', true, array['p-rp-lead','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-pf-03-aux","score":8.37,"terms":["component","cool"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-hu-02","score":5.2,"terms":["job","person"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-mp-01","score":4.19,"terms":["person","work"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-rp-02","score":3.77,"terms":["person","work"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-1","score":11.58,"terms":["check","component","redundant","train","work","wrong"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-2","score":3.71,"terms":["event","time"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-fs-dataquality","score":7.44,"terms":["order","packag","work"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-fs-plantdata","score":4.1,"terms":["order","work"],"decision":"rejected"}]'::jsonb, 'p-head-sq', 'w-mnt-01', 'cs-001', 'pos-w-mnt-01', 'Head of Supplier Quality (role card)', 'رئيس جودة الموردين (بطاقة دور)', 'Humaid Al Ketbi', 'حميد الكتبي', 'war_stories', 14, 1, '2026-06-15T11:00:00Z', '2026-06-22T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-06-13T10:00:00Z', '2026-06-22T09:00:00Z'),
('kas-002', 'Standing alarms: owner, work order and date', 'الإنذارات القائمة: مالك وأمر عمل وتاريخ', 'A control room practice for standing alarms: each has an owner, a work order and a date, the list is read aloud at turnover, and unexplained alarms are treated as new.', 'ممارسة في غرفة التحكم للإنذارات القائمة: لكل إنذار مالك وأمر عمل وتاريخ، وتُقرأ القائمة بصوت مسموع عند التسليم، ويُعامل الإنذار غير المفسَّر كإنذار جديد.', 'Standing alarms are the quiet problem in the control room. When an alarm stays lit for weeks, the crew stops seeing it, and then the real signal hides behind it. What I teach: every standing alarm has an owner, a work order and a date. At turnover we read the standing list out loud and ask what has changed since yesterday. If you cannot explain why an alarm is lit, treat it as new. The board is telling you something about the plant or about the instrument, and both matter. We also keep a short list of the alarms that tend to come in pairs, because when only one of the pair appears, that is usually an instrument problem rather than a process problem. The simulator is the place to practise this: we load a scenario with three nuisance alarms and one real one, and we watch who finds the real one first.', 'en', '[{"en":"Every standing alarm has an owner, a work order and a date.","ar":"لكل إنذار قائم مالك وأمر عمل وتاريخ."},{"en":"Read the standing list aloud at turnover and ask what changed.","ar":"اقرأ قائمة الإنذارات القائمة بصوت مسموع عند التسليم واسأل عما تغيّر."},{"en":"If you cannot explain why an alarm is lit, treat it as new.","ar":"إذا لم تستطع تفسير سبب إنذار مضاء فعامله كإنذار جديد."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-co-01']::text[], array['qs-ro','qs-sro']::text[], '{}'::text[], array['oe-3']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'human_performance', 'published', true, array['p-head-sq','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-3","score":6.24,"terms":["alarm","problem","stand"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-fs-systems","score":6.43,"terms":["real","see"],"decision":"rejected"}]'::jsonb, 'p-k-instructor', 'w-sro-02', 'cs-002', 'pos-w-sro-02', 'Simulator instructor (SRO-qualified)', 'مدرب المحاكي (مؤهل كمشغّل أول)', 'Maitha Al Suwaidi', 'ميثاء السويدي', 'rules_of_thumb', 11, 1, '2026-06-29T11:00:00Z', '2026-07-05T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-06-27T10:00:00Z', '2026-07-05T09:00:00Z'),
('kas-003', 'Place-keeping when the evolution feels familiar', 'تتبّع الخطوات حين يبدو الإجراء مألوفاً', 'How a shift supervisor keeps procedure use safe under time pressure: place-keeping on paper every time, restarting with a peer after an interruption, and stopping when anyone feels rushed.', 'كيف يحافظ مشرف الوردية على سلامة استخدام الإجراءات تحت ضغط الوقت: تتبّع الخطوات ورقياً في كل مرة، والاستئناف مع زميل بعد أي انقطاع، والتوقف عندما يشعر أي شخص بالاستعجال.', 'Time pressure is when steps get skipped. In the turbine building, the procedure is long and the evolution is familiar, which is exactly the trap. My practice is place-keeping on paper every time, even for the tenth repetition: circle the step, slash it when done. If somebody calls you away, you mark where you stopped and you restart from the last completed step with a peer, not from where you think you were. As a shift supervisor I would rather hold an evolution for ten minutes than recover from a missed step. The words I use with the crew are simple: if you feel rushed, say it, and we stop. Nobody has ever been criticised on my shift for stopping. The operating experience on skipped steps shows that the people involved were experienced and confident; that is why the habit matters more than the knowledge.', 'en', '[{"en":"Circle the step, slash it when done, every time.","ar":"ضع دائرة حول الخطوة واشطبها عند إنجازها، في كل مرة."},{"en":"After an interruption, restart from the last completed step with a peer.","ar":"بعد أي انقطاع، استأنف من آخر خطوة منجزة مع زميل."},{"en":"If you feel rushed, say it, and the crew stops.","ar":"إذا شعرت بالاستعجال فقل ذلك، ويتوقف الطاقم."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-hu-01','sk-co-03']::text[], array['qs-lo-turbine']::text[], '{}'::text[], array['oe-2']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'human_performance', 'published', true, array['p-k-instructor','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-2","score":14.75,"terms":["evolution","keep","miss","place","rush","skipp"],"decision":"accepted"}]'::jsonb, 'p-sro', 'w-ss-01', 'cs-003', 'pos-w-ss-01', 'Shift Manager · licensed SRO, Crew B (role card)', 'مدير الوردية · مشغّل أول مرخّص، الطاقم ب (بطاقة دور)', 'Saeed Al Ketbi', 'سعيد الكتبي', 'critical_decisions', 6, 1, '2026-07-13T11:00:00Z', '2026-07-19T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-07-11T10:00:00Z', '2026-07-19T09:00:00Z'),
('kas-004', 'Releasing tools from the controlled area', 'إخراج الأدوات من المنطقة المراقبة', 'Practical contamination control for tools: survey every tool before release, second survey for tools with crevices, keep a dedicated tool set inside and plan survey time into the job.', 'ضبط عملي للتلوث في الأدوات: مسح كل أداة قبل إخراجها، ومسح ثانٍ للأدوات ذات الشقوق، والاحتفاظ بمجموعة أدوات مخصصة في الداخل، وتخطيط وقت المسح ضمن العمل.', 'Tools leaving the radiologically controlled area are the most common way contamination travels. The rule is simple: every tool is surveyed before release, and anything with crevices gets a second survey after wiping. Hollow handles, ratchets and cable reels are the usual hiding places. We keep a separate set of tools inside the controlled area for the jobs we repeat, so that less moves across the boundary at all. When a job is planned, I ask the planner which tools will come out at the end and plan the survey time into the schedule, because a rushed survey at the end of a shift is where mistakes happen. If a survey reading is borderline, bag it, tag it and ask; do not average it away. The lesson from industry is that the contaminated tool was always one that someone assumed had been checked.', 'en', '[{"en":"Hollow handles, ratchets and cable reels are the usual hiding places.","ar":"المقابض المجوفة ومفاتيح السقاطة وبكرات الكابلات هي الأماكن المعتادة لاختباء التلوث."},{"en":"Plan survey time into the schedule; rushed surveys cause mistakes.","ar":"خطط لوقت المسح ضمن الجدول؛ فالمسح المستعجل يسبب الأخطاء."},{"en":"A borderline reading is bagged, tagged and asked about, never averaged away.","ar":"القراءة الحدّية تُعبّأ وتُوسم ويُسأل عنها، ولا يُلجأ إلى متوسطها."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-rp-01','sk-rp-02-survey']::text[], array['qs-rp']::text[], '{}'::text[], array['oe-5']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'radiation_protection', 'published', true, array['p-ep-manager','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-rp-02-survey","score":10.53,"terms":["contamination","survey"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-5","score":7.59,"terms":["contamination","survey","tool","tools"],"decision":"accepted"}]'::jsonb, 'p-rp-lead', 'w-rp-02', 'cs-004', 'pos-w-rp-02', 'Radiation Protection Team Leader (role card)', 'قائد فريق الوقاية من الإشعاع (بطاقة دور)', 'Fatima Al Mazrouei', 'فاطمة المزروعي', 'rules_of_thumb', 4, 1, '2026-07-20T11:00:00Z', '2026-07-26T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-07-18T10:00:00Z', '2026-07-26T09:00:00Z'),
('kas-005', 'Foreign material exclusion in a busy outage', 'منع المواد الغريبة خلال انقطاع مزدحم', 'Habits that keep open systems clean when dozens are open at once: boundary logs and covers, tethered tools, counts in and out, and a close-out inspection with a light and a mirror.', 'عادات تحافظ على نظافة الأنظمة المفتوحة حين يُفتح العشرات منها في وقت واحد: سجلات الحدود والأغطية، وربط الأدوات، والعدّ عند الدخول والخروج، والفحص النهائي بمصباح ومرآة.', 'Foreign material exclusion is about the open system, not the size of the job. Every time a system is opened, the boundary gets a log, a cover and a person responsible for it. During an outage we have dozens of open systems at once, and the worst finds come from the small jobs that nobody thought needed a full plan. My habits: tether small tools, count items in and out, and do the close-out inspection with a light and a mirror, not a glance. When something is missing from the count, we stop and search before closing, even if it is a washer. Work packages should say clearly which boundary class applies, so the crew does not have to decide in the field. Outage lessons show that foreign material was found later in pumps and valves; the cost of looking for ten more minutes is always smaller.', 'en', '[{"en":"Every open system gets a log, a cover and a person responsible.","ar":"لكل نظام مفتوح سجل وغطاء وشخص مسؤول."},{"en":"When the count is short, stop and search before closing.","ar":"عند نقص العدد، توقف وابحث قبل الإغلاق."},{"en":"Work packages state the boundary class, so the crew does not decide in the field.","ar":"تحدد حزم العمل فئة الحدود حتى لا يقرر الطاقم ذلك في الموقع."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-mp-01-mech']::text[], array['qs-mech']::text[], '{}'::text[], array['oe-4']::text[], '{}'::text[], 'outage', 'published', true, array['p-sq-lead','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-4","score":10.56,"terms":["exclusion","foreign","lesson","material","open","outage"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-5","score":2.55,"terms":["lesson","tools"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-fs-agents","score":4.38,"terms":["small","tools"],"decision":"rejected"}]'::jsonb, 'p-head-sq', 'w-mnt-02', 'cs-005', 'pos-w-mnt-02', 'Head of Supplier Quality (role card)', 'رئيس جودة الموردين (بطاقة دور)', 'Sultan Al Mazrouei', 'سلطان المزروعي', 'rules_of_thumb', 8, 1, '2026-08-03T11:00:00Z', '2026-08-08T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-08-01T10:00:00Z', '2026-08-08T09:00:00Z'),
('kas-006', 'Receiving inspection: item first, certificate second', 'فحص الاستلام: الصنف أولاً ثم الشهادة', 'How an inspector avoids being led by the paperwork: read the stamping on the item first, then match heat number, grade, size and quantity, and hold anything that does not match.', 'كيف يتجنب المفتش أن تقوده الأوراق: اقرأ الختم على الصنف أولاً، ثم طابق رقم الصهر والدرجة والمقاس والكمية، واحجز أي صنف لا يتطابق.', 'At receiving inspection the paperwork can look perfect and still be wrong. The certificate has to match the item in front of you: heat number, material grade, size and quantity. I check the stamping on the item first and only then read the certificate, so the paper does not lead my eye. Missing or mismatched heat numbers are the most common finding, and the supplier is usually cooperative once we show them exactly what does not match. Commercial grade items need the critical characteristics to be verified, not assumed. When in doubt, hold the item in the quarantine area and raise a nonconformance; never accept on a promise that the corrected certificate will follow. The supplier courses on counterfeit and suspect items are worth taking before your first year of inspections.', 'en', '[{"en":"Check the stamping on the item before reading the certificate.","ar":"افحص الختم على الصنف قبل قراءة الشهادة."},{"en":"Missing or mismatched heat numbers are the most common finding.","ar":"أرقام الصهر المفقودة أو غير المتطابقة هي الملاحظة الأكثر شيوعاً."},{"en":"Never accept on a promise that a corrected certificate will follow.","ar":"لا تقبل بناءً على وعد بأن الشهادة المصححة ستصل لاحقاً."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-qa-01','sk-qa-02-cgd']::text[], array['qs-qa']::text[], '{}'::text[], array['oe-6']::text[], array['c-sa-cgd-103','c-sa-cfsi-102']::text[], 'maintenance', 'published', true, array['p-head-sq','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-qa-02-cgd","score":10.21,"terms":["commercial","grade"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-qa-02","score":8.85,"terms":["commercial","grade"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-6","score":12.19,"terms":["certificate","heat","inspection","item","material","mismatch"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-sa-cgd-103","score":19.83,"terms":["characteristic","commercial","critical","grade","item"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-sa-cfsi-102","score":9.85,"terms":["items","suspect"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-fs-factoryqa","score":3.61,"terms":["inspection","supplier"],"decision":"rejected"}]'::jsonb, 'p-sq-lead', 'w-qa-01', 'cs-006', 'pos-w-qa-01', 'Supplier Quality Lead (role card)', 'قائد جودة الموردين (بطاقة دور)', 'Majid Al Ketbi', 'ماجد الكتبي', 'documents', 3, 1, '2026-08-17T11:00:00Z', '2026-08-23T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-08-15T10:00:00Z', '2026-08-23T09:00:00Z'),
('kas-007', 'Reading the steam generator blowdown trend', 'قراءة اتجاه تصريف مولد البخار', 'What the shape of the sodium, chloride and sulfate trends says about the secondary side, when to take a confirmatory sample and why each unit has its own normal.', 'ما الذي يكشفه شكل اتجاهات الصوديوم والكلوريد والكبريتات عن الدائرة الثانوية، ومتى تؤخذ عينة تأكيدية، ولماذا لكل وحدة نمطها الطبيعي.', 'Steam generator blowdown trends tell you about the health of the secondary side long before a limit is reached. I look at sodium, chloride and sulfate together, and I look at the shape of the trend rather than a single sample. A slow rise across several days usually points to condenser in-leakage, and the earlier you catch it, the smaller the clean-up. When a sample looks odd, take a confirmatory sample before you call the shift, but do not wait for the next routine sample. Keep the sample lines flushed for the full time, because a short flush gives you yesterday''s chemistry. New technicians should learn the normal pattern of each unit; the units are not identical, and what is normal on one can be early warning on the other.', 'en', '[{"en":"Read sodium, chloride and sulfate together and look at the shape of the trend.","ar":"اقرأ الصوديوم والكلوريد والكبريتات معاً وانظر إلى شكل الاتجاه."},{"en":"A slow rise over several days usually points to condenser in-leakage.","ar":"الارتفاع البطيء على مدى أيام يشير عادة إلى تسرب في المكثف."},{"en":"Flush sample lines for the full time.","ar":"اغسل خطوط العينات للمدة الكاملة."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-ch-01']::text[], array['qs-chem']::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'chemistry', 'review', false, '{}'::text[], '[]'::jsonb, 'p-chem-sup', 'w-chem-01', 'cs-007', 'pos-w-chem-01', 'Chemistry Supervisor (role card)', 'مشرف الكيمياء (بطاقة دور)', 'Sara Al Ketbi', 'سارة الكتبي', 'rules_of_thumb', 0, 1, '2026-09-07T11:00:00Z', null, null, null, null, '2026-09-05T10:00:00Z', '2026-09-07T11:00:00Z'),
('kas-008', 'What the startup curve tells you', 'ما الذي يخبرك به منحنى بدء التشغيل', 'Using the inverse count rate plot during startup: compare it with the predicted critical position, say the numbers aloud as a team and slow down to recalculate when they drift.', 'استخدام منحنى معدل العد العكسي أثناء بدء التشغيل: قارنه بالموضع الحرج المتوقع، ورددوا الأرقام بصوت مسموع كفريق، وتمهّلوا لإعادة الحساب عند الانحراف.', 'Reading the startup curve is a skill you build over many startups. The inverse count rate plot tells you how close you are to criticality, and the shape of it tells you whether the estimate is trustworthy. I always compare the predicted critical position with what the curve is doing and ask why if they differ by more than the expected band. Reactivity monitoring is a team sport: the reactor engineer, the operator at the controls and the shift supervisor should be saying the same numbers aloud. If the numbers start to drift from the prediction, slow down and recalculate rather than push on. Core physics tests after refuelling are where newcomers learn the most, so put them beside an experienced engineer for at least two cycles.', 'en', '[{"en":"Compare the predicted critical position with the curve and ask why they differ.","ar":"قارن الموضع الحرج المتوقع بالمنحنى واسأل عن سبب الاختلاف."},{"en":"Reactivity monitoring is a team activity: say the numbers aloud.","ar":"مراقبة التفاعلية نشاط جماعي: ردد الأرقام بصوت مسموع."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-pf-01-core']::text[], array['qs-sro']::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'reactor_core', 'review', false, '{}'::text[], '[{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-pf-01-core","score":8.19,"terms":["core","physic"],"decision":"pending"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-pf-01-advfuel","score":6.12,"terms":["core","physic"],"decision":"pending"}]'::jsonb, 'p-k-instructor', 'w-eng-05', 'cs-008', 'pos-w-eng-05', 'Simulator instructor (SRO-qualified)', 'مدرب المحاكي (مؤهل كمشغّل أول)', 'Yousef Al Suwaidi', 'يوسف السويدي', 'rules_of_thumb', 0, 1, '2026-10-05T11:00:00Z', null, null, null, null, '2026-09-19T10:00:00Z', '2026-10-05T11:00:00Z'),
('kas-009', 'Shift turnover: what the log does not say', 'تسليم الوردية: ما لا يُكتب في السجل', 'Face-to-face turnover at the boards, reading the standing alarms and open work aloud, and asking the incoming operator to explain the plant state in their own words.', 'التسليم وجهاً لوجه أمام اللوحات، وقراءة الإنذارات القائمة والأعمال المفتوحة بصوت مسموع، والطلب من المشغل القادم شرح حالة المحطة بكلماته.', 'تسليم الوردية هو اللحظة التي تنتقل فيها المعرفة من طاقم إلى طاقم، وأي معلومة لا تُقال في هذه اللحظة قد تضيع. قاعدتي أن يكون التسليم وجهاً لوجه أمام اللوحات، وأن نقرأ قائمة الإنذارات القائمة والأعمال المفتوحة بصوت مسموع. أطلب من المشغل القادم أن يعيد بكلماته ما فهمه عن حالة المحطة، فإذا لم يستطع شرح أمر ما، نتوقف ونوضحه قبل التوقيع. المعلومات المكتوبة مهمة، لكن السياق لا يُكتب دائماً: لماذا أجّلنا عملاً معيناً، ومن ينتظر ماذا. أنصح المشرفين الجدد بأن يخصصوا وقتاً كافياً للتسليم حتى في الأيام الهادئة، لأن العادة تُبنى في الأيام الهادئة وتُختبر في الأيام الصعبة.', 'ar', '[{"en":"Turnover happens face to face at the boards.","ar":"يتم التسليم وجهاً لوجه أمام اللوحات."},{"en":"The incoming operator explains the plant state in their own words.","ar":"يشرح المشغل القادم حالة المحطة بكلماته."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-co-01']::text[], array['qs-ro']::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'human_performance', 'draft', false, '{}'::text[], '[]'::jsonb, 'p-sro', 'w-ss-02', 'cs-009', 'pos-w-ss-02', 'Shift Manager · licensed SRO, Crew B (role card)', 'مدير الوردية · مشغّل أول مرخّص، الطاقم ب (بطاقة دور)', 'Chinedu Okafor', 'Chinedu Okafor', 'critical_decisions', 0, 1, null, null, null, null, null, '2026-09-26T10:00:00Z', '2026-09-28T11:00:00Z'),
('kas-010', 'What the drill controller looks for', 'ما الذي يبحث عنه مراقب التمرين', 'Communication over heroics in emergency drills: repeat-backs, a log that keeps up, announcing actions before taking them and a critique that starts with what the team saw.', 'التواصل قبل البطولات في تمارين الطوارئ: التكرار للتأكيد، وسجل يواكب الأحداث، والإعلان عن الإجراءات قبل تنفيذها، ونقد يبدأ بما رآه الفريق.', 'In an emergency drill the controller is looking for communication, not heroics. The first thing I watch is whether the crew repeats back the messages and whether the log keeps up with events. Good teams announce what they are about to do before they do it, so everyone can catch a mistake. I also watch how the team handles the second injected problem, because the first one is usually well rehearsed. After the drill, the critique should start with what the team saw, not with what the controller saw. This approach has been replaced by the updated drill guide, which now covers the same points with the new scenario set.', 'en', '[{"en":"Watch how the team handles the second injected problem.","ar":"راقب كيف يتعامل الفريق مع المشكلة الثانية المضافة."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-ep-01']::text[], array['qs-ero']::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'emergency_preparedness', 'withdrawn', false, array['p-head-sq','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[]'::jsonb, 'p-ep-manager', 'w-ep-01', 'cs-010', 'pos-w-ep-01', 'Emergency Preparedness Manager (role card)', 'مدير التأهب للطوارئ (بطاقة دور)', 'Humaid Al Ketbi', 'حميد الكتبي', 'war_stories', 0, 1, '2026-05-25T11:00:00Z', '2026-05-31T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', '2026-09-30T12:00:00Z', 'Replaced by the updated drill guide and scenario set', '2026-05-23T10:00:00Z', '2026-09-30T12:00:00Z'),
('kas-011', 'Design basis: why the margins are where they are', 'أساس التصميم: لماذا الهوامش حيث هي', 'An engineer explains how design margins are set from the design basis, why changes go through configuration control, and which questions to ask before proposing a modification.', 'يشرح مهندس كيف تُحدَّد هوامش التصميم من أساس التصميم، ولماذا تمر التغييرات عبر ضبط التهيئة، وما الأسئلة التي تُطرح قبل اقتراح أي تعديل.', 'Design margins are not arbitrary. Each one traces back to the design basis: the events the plant must withstand and the assumptions in the safety analysis. When someone proposes a change, the first question is which design basis document sets the margin, and the second is what analysis would need to be redone. Configuration control exists so that the plant as built, the documents and the analysis stay in agreement. A modification that is small in the field can be large on paper, and the paper is what the next engineer will rely on. Before proposing a modification, talk to the system engineer, read the design basis and the calculation, and write down your assumptions so that a reviewer can check them.', 'en', '[{"en":"Every margin traces back to a design basis document; find it before you change anything.","ar":"كل هامش يعود إلى وثيقة أساس تصميم؛ اعثر عليها قبل تغيير أي شيء."},{"en":"Configuration control protects the people who come after you.","ar":"ضبط التهيئة يحمي من يأتون بعدك."}]'::jsonb, array['sk-en-02','sk-en-01','sk-en-01-mods']::text[], array['qs-eng']::text[], '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], array['c-eng-init']::text[], 'primary', 'published', true, array['p-head-sq','p-training-mgr']::text[], '[{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-en-01-mods","score":17.98,"terms":["configuration","control","design","modification","plant"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-en-01-project","score":13.92,"terms":["configuration","control","design","engineer"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-en-01","score":10.96,"terms":["configuration","control","design"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-da-01-scripting","score":9.59,"terms":["analysi","engineer"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"skill","ref":"sk-pf-03-aux","score":6.56,"terms":["control","plant","system"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"oe","ref":"oe-4","score":2.27,"terms":["control","system"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-eng-init","score":15.38,"terms":["basis","configuration","design","engineer"],"decision":"accepted"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-fs-plantlit-x","score":6.13,"terms":["control","plant","system"],"decision":"rejected"},{"kind":"course","ref":"c-loit-sys","score":5.39,"terms":["plant","system"],"decision":"rejected"}]'::jsonb, 'p-sme-reviewer', 'p-sme-reviewer', null, 'pos-p-sme-reviewer', 'SME reviewer (role card)', 'مراجع خبير (بطاقة دور)', 'SME reviewer (role card)', 'مراجع خبير (بطاقة دور)', null, 5, 1, '2026-08-20T11:00:00Z', '2026-08-28T09:00:00Z', 'p-training-mgr', null, null, '2026-08-18T10:00:00Z', '2026-08-28T09:00:00Z')
